ons to Hold Us Back de Public Enemy: bucles de ruido puro que llevaron el funk a la era digital, ataques a la industria y a los cantantes «sin espina», la oratoria de Chuck D y el bufón consciente Flavor Flav, con su reloj. «Fight the Power» (Do the Right Thing, 1989) quería, según Greg Tate, reconvocar el Black Power con el hip hop como medio; para Clinton eran lo que Dylan fue para el rock.","color":"#94a3b8","family":"Hip hop, go-go y funk de los noventa","link":"https://volteret4.github.io/Funk/#rap-politico"}],"book_tracks":[{"id":230310505875741,"artist":"The Boys","artist_id":98797607334115,"title":"Thanx 4 the Funk","year":1990,"ess":0,"yt":"L2c7VzS6YAQ","kind":null,"book":{"id":4,"title":"Funk: The Music, the People, and the Rhythm of the One","author":"Rickey Vincent","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/Funk/"},"scene":"Rap político: Public Enemy y Boogie Down Productions","scene_id":171935738366324,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/Funk/#rap-politico","chapters":["Cap. 21: Funk in the Nineties: Return of the Funk"],"pages":[]}],"mentions":[{"book":"Funk: The Music, the People, and the Rhythm of the One","author":"Rickey Vincent","page":292,"text":"…GO At first glance looking like nothing more than large and loud R&B acts onstage, Go Go bands such as Trouble Funk, E.U., Rare Essence, Redds and the Boys, and their mentor Chuck Brown & the Soul Searchers, delivered the strongest, hottest, truest monster funk experience of the decade. Storming the…"},{"book":"Funk: The Music, the People, and the Rhythm of the One","author":"Rickey Vincent","page":293,"text":"…music. Locked into the endless funk groove, mimicking the dialogue on pop tunes and P-Funk hits, bands such as Trouble Funk, Rare Essence, Redds and the Boys, and E.U. were going strong by 1984. (It is important to note that anything can be played over a Go Go beat, and for three hours a night, everything…"}],"podcast":[],"awards":[],"concerts":[],"xref":[],"charts":[{"id":79669917374341,"type":"a